            "body": "The new predicate allows a projection containing Present token/developer diagnostics to be canonical and checkpointed, but apply_batch_with_completeness still clears every projection diagnostic for any complete canonical batch (line 707). Same-source append restores that reducer state and only adapts the delta; an unchanged-source append has no events to rebuild the diagnostics. Reproduced via the current formal target process: initial backfill has token_usage_record=1/developer_message_hidden=1; checkpoint restart plus no-growth append drops both to 0 in batch.projection and complete.checkpoint.reducer_state while still reporting completed/canonical. Growth append from the original anchor also drops both. Known diagnostic evidence is therefore lost on normal recovery/continuation; the new test only checks a later partial overlap and does not cover another canonical batch. Preserve committed Present diagnostics with stable identity/dedup across canonical delta/replay, while retaining fail-closed unknown/partial cleanup; extend the existing append/restart regression.",
